From 50a3074da5d74344b5a4465c3ea9f5b815b9d287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:34:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Journey background trip: lake loop keeps its crossfade
 aligned across hide/return; test locks the cutscene audio resume
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Voice Bot: with the cutscene now resuming by itself on return (2c12565), its sound must come back where it was.
On this line the island→lakeside journey has no cue / voice track and no cue timing.json (the only timeline track,
audio_cine/sfx_exit_outbound, is the home exit's, with its own restart rule). Its sound is the bed: amb_lake_loop
on the arrival stretch plus the GameAudio loops (wind / waves / BGM), which suspend('hidden') pauses and resumes.

Fix (LakeAmbienceCore.step): when the lake read as not wanted while silent, a running loop crossfade stopped its
partner (reset to 0). A background trip reads as not wanted (snapshot state 'paused'), so hiding inside the 0.2 s
crossfade window restarted the partner at 0 against cur on return: a 50 ms misaligned crossfade. Both sources are
now only paused (they already are by the silent branch) and the crossfade resumes aligned; the existing partner
timeout still covers a partner that never plays again.

Test journey-background-audio (in run-suite): hide at 2 s, 9.5 s, mid-crossfade (loopS+0.05, loopS+delay+0.08) and
30 s, hidden 0.5-10 s, then the paused-visible frame and the auto-resumed arrival: lake loop paused not stopped
(position kept), resumes from that position (offset <= 50 ms, measured 0), never two sources outside the crossfade,
full level after the fade-in; muted/gated silent with no drift; still exactly 3 sfxMuted gates (none added);
tripwire: a journey cue track or cue timing.json added later fails this test until it gets timeline-synced resume.
